{
  "id": "ep045",
  "duration": 56.934,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 6.452,
      "text": "NASA intentionally crashed a three-billion-dollar spacecraft into Saturn's crushing atmosphere.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Cassini proximals overhead.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cassini_proximals_overhead.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 6.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 6.452,
      "end": 13.672,
      "text": "The Cassini-Huygens mission, a joint international effort, arrived at the ringed planet in July 2004.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Saturn Prior to Cassini Probe's Arrival (2004-18-1545).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA and E. Karkoschka (University of Arizona)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn_Prior_to_Cassini_Probe%27s_Arrival_(2004-18-1545).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 6.467,
          "end": 9.567,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 9.567,
          "end": 13.667,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 13.672,
      "end": 20.842,
      "text": "The spacecraft discovered geysers of water ice on Enceladus and methane seas on the massive moon Titan.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Dramatic plumes, both large and small, spray water ice out from many locations along the famed tiger stripes near the south pole of Saturn\u2019s moon Enceladus in this image released on Feb 23 (newly-found-organics-in-enceladus-plumes).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech/Space Science Institute",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dramatic_plumes,_both_large_and_small,_spray_water_ice_out_from_many_locations_along_the_famed_tiger_stripes_near_the_south_pole_of_Saturn%E2%80%99s_moon_Enceladus_in_this_image_released_on_Feb_23_(newly-found-organics-in-enceladus-plumes).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 13.667,
          "end": 20.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 20.842,
      "end": 26.437,
      "text": "These worlds had everything needed for life, but Cassini was running out of rocket fuel.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 20.833,
          "end": 26.433,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 26.437,
      "end": 33.832,
      "text": "Scientists realized if the dead probe ever drifted and crashed, Earthly microbes could contaminate these pristine moons.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA22912.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA22912.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 26.433,
          "end": 33.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 33.832,
      "end": 41.052,
      "text": "To prevent a biological disaster, they ordered a 'Grand Finale' dive through the rings and into Saturn's clouds.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Cassini Grand Finale.png",
        "credit": "NASA / JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cassini_Grand_Finale.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 33.833,
          "end": 41.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 41.052,
      "end": 49.702,
      "text": "On September 15, 2017, Cassini fought Saturn's winds for 30 seconds longer than predicted before burning up.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Cassini's final plunge 7635 CGF STILL 00032.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cassini%27s_final_plunge_7635_CGF_STILL_00032.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 41.067,
          "end": 46.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 46.067,
          "end": 49.7,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 49.702,
      "end": 56.584,
      "text": "This was a calculated sacrifice to protect moons that might hold life from the three-billion-dollar spacecraft.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Cassini proximals overhead.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cassini_proximals_overhead.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 49.7,
          "end": 56.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
